{"slug":"clean-up","title":"Stop, shut down and clean up","description":"Three levels of tidying, from deleting namespaces to removing the cluster and its kubectl context.","order":8,"tags":["kind","k3d"],"date":"2026-10-14","minutes":6,"words":493,"toc":[{"depth":2,"id":"part-1--delete-the-namespaces-the-cluster-stays","text":"Part 1 — Delete the namespaces (the cluster stays)"},{"depth":2,"id":"part-2--stop-the-cluster-and-start-it-again","text":"Part 2 — Stop the cluster and start it again"},{"depth":2,"id":"part-3--complete-shutdown","text":"Part 3 — Complete shutdown"}],"html":"<p>For the kind cluster <code>local-cluster-1</code>; for a k3d cluster see the last section of\n<a href=\"/blog/k3d-cluster\">Create a local Kubernetes cluster with k3d</a>. Three levels, from lightest to complete. Pick the one you\nneed.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Table (scrolls sideways)\"><table><thead><tr><th>You want</th><th>Level</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Free memory for a while, keep everything</td><td>Part 2: stop the cluster</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Empty the cluster, keep the cluster</td><td>Part 1: delete the namespaces</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Remove everything this guide made</td><td>Part 3: complete shutdown</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"part-1--delete-the-namespaces-the-cluster-stays\"><a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#part-1--delete-the-namespaces-the-cluster-stays\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a>Part 1 — Delete the namespaces (the cluster stays)</h2>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kubectl%20delete%20namespace%20web%20cache%20db%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kubectl delete namespace web cache db</code></pre></figure>\n<p>Deletes the namespaces and everything inside them: Deployments, pods, Services. The cluster and its nodes\nkeep running, empty.</p>\n<h2 id=\"part-2--stop-the-cluster-and-start-it-again\"><a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#part-2--stop-the-cluster-and-start-it-again\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a>Part 2 — Stop the cluster and start it again</h2>\n<p>kind has no stop command, but its nodes are Docker containers, so stop those. Everything inside the cluster\nis kept:</p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22docker%20stop%20%24(kind%20get%20nodes%20--name%20local-cluster-1)%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>docker stop $(kind get nodes --name local-cluster-1)</code></pre></figure>\n<p><code>kind get nodes</code> prints the three node names; <code>docker stop</code> stops each one. The memory is freed.</p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22docker%20ps%20--format%20'table%20%7B%7B.Names%7D%7D%5C%5Ct%7B%7B.Status%7D%7D'%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>docker ps --format <span class=\"hljs-string\">&#x27;table {{.Names}}\\t{{.Status}}&#x27;</span></code></pre></figure>\n<p>The three <code>local-cluster-1-…</code> containers are gone from the running list.</p>\n<p>To bring it back:</p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22docker%20start%20%24(kind%20get%20nodes%20--name%20local-cluster-1)%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>docker start $(kind get nodes --name local-cluster-1)</code></pre></figure>\n<p>Wait a minute or two, then:</p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kubectl%20get%20nodes%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kubectl get nodes</code></pre></figure>\n<p>All three <code>Ready</code> (they show <code>NotReady</code> for a short while). Your namespaces and deployments are still there;\ntheir pods restart on their own.</p>\n<h2 id=\"part-3--complete-shutdown\"><a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#part-3--complete-shutdown\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a>Part 3 — Complete shutdown</h2>\n<p>Do these in order. Each removes one layer; stop wherever you like.</p>\n<p><strong>1. Delete the cluster</strong> (the three node containers and everything inside):</p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kind%20delete%20cluster%20--name%20local-cluster-1%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kind delete cluster --name local-cluster-1</code></pre></figure>\n<p>kind also removes the cluster&#39;s entries from <code>~/.kube/config</code>: the context, cluster and user, all named\n<code>kind-local-cluster-1</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>2. Check what kubectl still lists:</strong></p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kubectl%20config%20get-contexts%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kubectl config get-contexts</code></pre></figure>\n<p><code>kind-local-cluster-1</code> should be gone. If it is still listed, it is a stale entry: this happens when the\ncluster was removed another way (for example its containers were deleted with <code>docker rm</code>, so kind never\ncleaned the file). Remove it by hand. A context is only a pointer, so deleting it never touches a cluster:</p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kubectl%20config%20delete-context%20kind-local-cluster-1%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kubectl config delete-context kind-local-cluster-1</code></pre></figure>\n<p>Read the exact name from the <code>NAME</code> column first, and never delete a cloud context (<code>gke_…</code>) you still use.\nIf the cluster and user entries are also left behind, remove them too (they share the context&#39;s name):</p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kubectl%20config%20delete-cluster%20kind-local-cluster-1%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kubectl config delete-cluster kind-local-cluster-1</code></pre></figure>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kubectl%20config%20delete-user%20kind-local-cluster-1%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kubectl config delete-user kind-local-cluster-1</code></pre></figure>\n<p><strong>3. Pick a current context on purpose.</strong> If the deleted one was current, kubectl now has none:</p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kubectl%20config%20current-context%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kubectl config current-context</code></pre></figure>\n<p>An error <code>current-context is not set</code> means exactly that. Choose one, or leave it empty until you need it:</p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kubectl%20config%20use-context%20%3Cthe%20context%20you%20want%3E%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kubectl config use-context &lt;the context you want&gt;</code></pre></figure>\n<p><strong>4. Remove the registry</strong>, if you made one in Part 1.2 of <a href=\"/blog/run-your-image\">Run your own image in the cluster</a> (this deletes every image pushed to it):</p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22docker%20rm%20-f%20kind-registry%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>docker <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">rm</span> -f kind-registry</code></pre></figure>\n<p><strong>5. Check nothing is left in Docker:</strong></p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22docker%20ps%20-a%20--format%20'table%20%7B%7B.Names%7D%7D%5C%5Ct%7B%7B.Status%7D%7D'%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>docker ps -a --format <span class=\"hljs-string\">&#x27;table {{.Names}}\\t{{.Status}}&#x27;</span></code></pre></figure>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kind%20get%20clusters%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kind get clusters</code></pre></figure>\n<p>No <code>local-cluster-1-…</code> or <code>kind-registry</code> containers, and <code>kind get clusters</code> does not list\n<code>local-cluster-1</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>6. Delete the files you wrote</strong> (optional):</p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"hljs-built_in\">rm</span> kind-config.yaml</code></pre></figure>\n<p><strong>7. Free the disk</strong> (optional). The node image stays in Docker&#39;s cache:</p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>docker image <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">rm</span> kindest/node:&lt;tag&gt;</code></pre></figure>\n<p>Find the tag with <code>docker image ls | grep kindest</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>8. Quit Docker Desktop</strong> (optional) to free memory: menu-bar whale icon → Quit Docker Desktop. With the\ncluster deleted, nothing is left running.</p>\n<p><strong>9clean everything</strong> clean unused resources at once (asks first, removes all stopped containers and dangling images):</p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22docker%20system%20prune%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>docker system prune</code></pre></figure>\n"}